.TH CRONEN 1 2026-10-24 cronen "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cronen \- see what pacman \-Syu is about to do before you run it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cronen
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-check " | " \-\-json " [" \-\-waybar ]]
.br
.B cronen
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.B install
.IR package ...
.br
.B cronen
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cronen
is a terminal UI for Arch Linux that shows pending repo and AUR updates,
the Arch news you haven't read, anything that needs manual intervention,
and risky packages (kernel, GPU drivers, glibc, systemd), with links to
upstream and the packaging changelog.
When you're happy, it hands the terminal to
.B sudo pacman \-Syu
or your AUR helper.
.PP
cronen only reads.
It never runs
.BR "pacman \-Sy" ,
so it can't cause a partial upgrade: pending updates come from
.BR checkupdates (8),
which syncs a temporary copy of the database.
.PP
An update is flagged when unread news mentions it or its pkgbase, when an
unread post requires manual intervention, when it matches the watchlist,
when its major version changes, when Python's minor version changes (AUR
packages depending on it likely need rebuilding), or when it is a kernel
(reboot afterwards).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print a short plain-text summary, most important first, and exit with a
status from
.B EXIT STATUS
below.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a one-line JSON summary, for example
.br
.nf
{"updates":18,"aur":2,"flagged":11,"acknowledged":0,"critical":1,"unread_news":2,"pacnew":1,"reboot":true,"download_bytes":929069795,"size_delta_bytes":27053259,"new":2,"replaced":1,"held":1,"security_fixes":2,"vulnerable":1,"preflight":[],"reboot_pending":false}
.fi
.I updates
counts repo and AUR updates together,
.I critical
counts unread news requiring manual intervention,
.I download_bytes
and
.I size_delta_bytes
are the transaction preview's download and installed\-size change,
.I new
counts packages the upgrade pulls in (replacements included),
.I replaced
the installed packages a replacement removes and
.I held
the updates held back by IgnorePkg,
.I security_fixes
the security advisories the pending updates fix,
.I vulnerable
the installed packages affected by an advisory no version fixes yet, and an
.I errors
array lists any source that failed.
.TP
.B \-\-waybar
With
.BR \-\-json ,
print
.IR text ,
.IR tooltip ,
.I class
and
.I alt
for a waybar custom module.
The class is one of
.BR none ,
.BR updates ,
.BR attention ,
.B critical
or
.BR error .
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Use bundled sample data and touch nothing on the system: no config, state
or cache is read or written, and upgrading runs nothing.
Also works with
.B \-\-check
and
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP 14
.BR j / k ", " \(da / \(ua
Move.
.TP
.BR g / G
Top / bottom.
.TP
.BR ctrl+d / ctrl+u
Half a page down / up in the detail or news pane.
.TP
.B tab
Switch focus between panes.
.TP
.B /
Filter the package list;
.B enter
keeps the filter,
.B esc
clears it.
.TP
.BR 1 ... 5
Switch screen: Updates, News, Packages, History, Housekeeping. The last two are
not built yet.
.TP
.B s
On the updates screen: sort by download size.
.TP
.B space
On the updates screen: mark the selected installed package for removal.
.TP
.B X
On the updates screen: remove the marked packages (dry run and confirmation first).
.TP
.B F
On the updates screen: prefetch, run
.B checkupdates \-d
(or
.BR prefetch_command )
to download the pending packages now (confirmation first).
.TP
.B I
On the updates screen: the install helper ("I need X now"). Offers the full upgrade plus
the package, or (with
.BR archive_install )
the package as of the last full upgrade. It never runs
.B pacman \-Sy
or
.B pacman \-S
against the real database.
.TP
.B n
News screen.
.TP
.B f
Packages screen: cycle what is listed (all, explicit, dependencies, foreign,
orphans).
.TP
.B s
Packages screen: cycle the sort (name, size, install date).
.TP
.B space
Packages screen: mark the selected package. Nothing acts on marks yet.
.TP
.B m
Mark the selected news item read (on the updates screen: the news behind
the selected package's flags).
.TP
.B o
Open the upstream URL (on the news screen: the post) with
.BR xdg\-open (1).
.TP
.B c
Open the packaging changelog.
.TP
.B d
Review the PKGBUILD diff of the selected pending AUR update.
.TP
.B a
Acknowledge every non-critical flag on the selected package, for its exact new
version. It moves to its normal group with a check mark; a newer version, or a
rule you had not acknowledged, flags it again. Critical flags (manual
intervention news) cannot be acknowledged. Acknowledged flags are ignored by
\fB\-\-check\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR and the exit codes.
.TP
.B A
Show or hide acknowledged packages.
.TP
.B r
Refresh everything, bypassing the cache.
.TP
.B U
Upgrade: confirm with
.BR y ,
then cronen suspends and runs the upgrade command.
Afterwards it reloads everything and shows the number of
.I .pacnew
files and whether to reboot.
Only a successful upgrade (exit status 0) marks the news up to now as read.
.TP
.B ?
Help.
.TP
.BR q ", " ctrl+c
Quit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is TOML.
A missing file is fine, every key is optional, and cronen never writes to
it.
.TP
.BR aur " (default " true )
Check the AUR for updates of foreign packages.
.TP
.BR aur_helper " (default " """""" )
.B paru
or
.B yay
to upgrade with
.B paru \-Syu
or
.B yay \-Syu
instead of
.BR "sudo pacman \-Syu" .
.TP
.B upgrade_command
A command line that overrides the above, split on whitespace.
.TP
.B watchlist
Package globs to always flag.
The defaults are
.IR linux* ,
.IR nvidia* ,
.IR mesa ,
.IR vulkan\-* ,
.IR glibc ,
.IR systemd ,
.IR grub ,
.IR pacman ,
.IR openssl ,
.I python
and
.IR gcc* .
.TP
.BR watchlist_mode " (default " extend )
.B extend
adds
.B watchlist
to the defaults;
.B replace
uses it alone.
.TP
.BR news_days " (default " 30 )
When the last upgrade is unknown, news from this many days counts as
unread.
.TP
.B ignore_major
Globs, matched against name and pkgbase, whose major version bumps aren't
flagged.
.TP
.BR show_debug " (default " false )
List makepkg
.I <name>\-debug
splits.
.TP
.BR preview " (default " true )
Show what an upgrade would do: new, replaced and held packages, the download
size and the change in installed size. It reads the database
.B checkupdates
synced (\fB$CHECKUPDATES_DB\fR, or \fB${TMPDIR:\-/tmp}/checkup\-db\-\fIUID\fR) with
.B pacman \-Sup \-\-dbpath
and never writes to the real database. A failed preview makes
.B \-\-check
exit 1 like any other failed source.
.TP
.BR flag_fresh_hours " (default " 0 )
Flag updates whose new build is younger than this many hours. 0 never flags.
.TP
.BR preflight " (default " true )
Check the system before an upgrade: /boot declared in fstab but not mounted
while a kernel updates, free space on /, the pacman cache and /boot against
what the upgrade needs, the pacman database lock, a pending reboot and an old
archlinux\-keyring. Problems are shown as a banner and in
.BR \-\-check ,
and the json output lists them in
.IR preflight .
cronen only reports them. A critical problem makes
.B \-\-check
exit 30.
.TP
.BR mirror_check " (default " true )
As part of the preflight checks, compare the first http(s) mirror in
/etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist with the reference mirror (geo.mirror.pkgbuild.com)
by their
.I lastupdate
files. A mirror that can't be reached makes
.B \-\-check
exit 1 like any other failed source.
.TP
.BR mirror_lag_hours " (default " 6 )
How far behind the reference mirror the mirror may be before it is reported.
.TP
.BR security " (default " true )
Check security.archlinux.org: mark updates that fix an advisory (they are a
reason to upgrade and never count as flagged) and count installed packages that
an unfixed advisory affects. The tracker can lag. With this off cronen makes no
request to it.
.TP
.BR known_issues " (default " true )
Look up open issues on the Arch packaging GitLab for pending repo updates, since
their new build, and flag the update. With this off cronen makes no request to
GitLab.
.TP
.BR package_browser " (default " true )
Read every installed package once per load (with
.BR "pacman \-Qi" ,
.B "pacman \-Qm"
and
.BR "pacman \-Qdtq" )
for the Packages screen. With this off cronen runs none of them.
.TP
.BR privilege_command " (default " sudo )
.BR sudo ", " doas " or " run0 .
Prefixes every write action and the default upgrade command.
.TP
.BR protected " (default empty), " protected_mode " (default " extend )
Package globs that can't be removed with a single
.BR y :
the confirm modal asks for the package name. In
.B extend
mode they are added to base, linux*, glibc, systemd, pacman, sudo, grub and systemd-boot*;
.B replace
uses only yours.
.TP
.BR extra_cache_dirs " (default empty)"
Globs of package cache directories besides pacman's CacheDir, shown on the Housekeeping screen.
.TP
.BR pacdiff_command " (default empty)"
Replaces
.IR "privilege_command pacdiff" .
.TP
.BR housekeeping " (default " true )
The Housekeeping screen's own reads: .pacnew diffs, the cache size and failed units.
.TP
.BR aur_review " (default " lazy )
.B lazy
fetches the PKGBUILD diff of a pending AUR update when it is opened with
.BR d ;
.B eager
fetches it for every pending AUR update, which also makes
.B \-\-check
and
.B \-\-json
evaluate the suspicious\-change rule.
.TP
.BR metered_warn_mib " (default " 100 )
Raise a preflight warning when NetworkManager calls the connection metered and the
download is bigger than this many MiB. 0 turns the check off.
.TP
.BR prefetch_command " (default empty)"
Replaces
.B checkupdates \-d
for the prefetch key. Split on whitespace and run as written: add
.B sudo
yourself if it needs it.
.TP
.BR archive_install " (default false)"
Turn on option B of the install helper (experimental): install a repository package
from the Arch Linux Archive snapshot of the day of the last full upgrade. Needs
.BR fakeroot .
Off unless set to true.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
aur_helper = "paru"
watchlist = ["zfs*"]
ignore_major = ["firefox"]
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
For
.BR \-\-check :
.TP 5
.B 0
Nothing to do.
.TP
.B 10
Updates available.
.TP
.B 20
Attention needed: at least one update is flagged. Acknowledged flags don't count.
.TP
.B 30
Critical: an unread news item requires manual intervention, or a preflight
check found a critical problem (an unmounted or full /boot, or too little free
space for the upgrade). Before this version, only the news case exited 30.
.TP
.B 1
Error: a source (checkupdates, the AUR, the news feed) failed.
With a source missing, cronen can't tell
.I nothing to do
from
.IR "didn't look" .
An unreadable
.I pacman.log
is not an error.
.PP
.B \-\-json
exits 0 once it has printed.
Invalid flags exit 2.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cronen/config.toml
Config, default
.IR ~/.config/cronen/config.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cronen/state.json
Read news and the last upgrade cronen ran, default
.IR ~/.local/state/cronen/state.json .
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cronen/
The news feed and AUR responses, kept for 15 minutes, default
.IR ~/.cache/cronen/ .
.TP
.I /var/log/pacman.log
Read for the time of the last full system upgrade.
If it is unreadable, the last upgrade is unknown and news from the last
.B news_days
days counts as unread.
.SH EXAMPLES
A waybar module:
.PP
.RS
.nf
"custom/cronen": {
    "exec": "cronen \-\-json \-\-waybar",
    "return\-type": "json",
    "interval": 1800,
    "on\-click": "foot \-e cronen"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
checkupdates syncs a temporary database from your mirror on every run, so
don't poll often.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR checkupdates (8),
.BR pacdiff (8),
.BR paru (8),
.BR yay (8)
.PP
https://github.com/leNITHISH/cronen
